    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is well-placed overall \u2014 the new CITY3 + per-city-sequence logic belongs in `AssignCustomerCode`, and `AssignMembershipNumber` correctly needed only a Javadoc/example update because it derives from the already-assigned `customerCode` (no logic duplication introduced there). One structural nit:\n\n- **Duplicated prefix-extraction in `AssignCustomerCode.service`:** the transform `x.substring(0, Math.min(3, x.length())).toUpperCase()` now appears twice \u2014 once for `city`, once for `lastName`:\n  ```java\n  String cityPrefix = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length())).toUpperCase();\n  ...\n  String lastPrefix = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();\n  ```\n  The old code had a single occurrence; the new format introduces a second identical derivation. Extract a small private helper to keep the \"upper-cased first three letters\" rule in one place, e.g.:\n  ```java\n  private static String prefix3(String value) {\n      return value.substring(0, Math.min(3, value.length())).toUpperCase();\n  }\n  ```\n  then `prefix3(city)` / `prefix3(lastName)`. This removes the duplication and names the shared concept, so a future format tweak (e.g. 4-letter prefixes) changes one line rather than two.\n\nEverything else (OpenAPI descriptions/examples, Javadoc updates, per-city filtering via the stream) reads naturally for this codebase.",
